{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":24697,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"be16fba1080da535f137e6cdbef62298b907019911f9c4a6e59d7dbe7fde1de4","packTokens":9974,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":41,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spec","tokens":9697,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nState, as numbered plain sentences (n = 1, 2, ...), what change this spec asks for. Don't add anything the spec doesn't say. Don't mention IDs.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spec\" kind=\"spec\" sha=\"\">\n{\n \"requirements\": [\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide role-oriented portal pages and navigation for stock, orders, deliveries, temperature monitoring, quality decisions, and recalls on phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A signed-in staff or customer user has portal access when the user opens portal navigation then the screen shows links to the modules permitted for that user, including applicable stock, order, delivery, temperature, quality, and recall pages\",\n    \"Given A user opens an available workflow at phone, tablet, and desktop viewport widths when the page is rendered then the screen content has no horizontal overflow and phone controls have touch targets of at least 44 by 44 CSS pixels\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide staff authentication through Meridian Microsoft accounts and customer authentication using email and password followed by a one-time code, with reset links requested by email and no social sign-in or single-sign-on option for customer accounts.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A staff user opens staff sign-in when the user selects the staff sign-in flow then the screen shows the Meridian Microsoft sign-in option and no external staff-account form\",\n    \"Given The API returns a one-time-code challenge after a customer submits email and password when the customer submits the credentials then the screen shows a code-entry field, no customer social sign-in or single-sign-on option, and no customer account content before a successful code response\",\n    \"Given A customer user requests a password reset when the reset request is submitted then the request contains the customer email address and the screen shows the reset-link-by-email confirmation returned by the API\",\n    \"Given A disabled or removed account attempts online sign-in or access when the API returns an access-denied response then the screen shows an access-denied message and no protected page or record is displayed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a user opens portal views, the Meridian responsive web app shall show records and actions returned for that user's role, assigned warehouses, and customer organisation, present Auditor views as read-only, and clear protected data when the API refuses access.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API returns records for a staff member's assigned warehouses or a customer's organisation when the user opens the corresponding list then the screen shows only the returned records\",\n    \"Given A Quality Manager or Auditor opens a warehouse-scoped list and the API returns all-warehouse records when the list is displayed then the screen shows the returned records from all warehouses\",\n    \"Given An Auditor opens a record page when the page renders then the screen shows record details without create, edit, or delete controls, and an API-refused write is shown as an error message\",\n    \"Given A protected request is refused because the account or record is inaccessible when the web app receives the refusal then the screen shows an access-ended or access-denied message and clears protected record fields\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let a Customer Administrator invite and remove users through controls scoped to that administrator's customer organisation.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Customer Administrator opens user management for their organisation when the administrator submits an invitation or removal then the screen shows the invitation or removal status returned by the API\",\n    \"Given The API refuses a user-management action, including an action for another organisation when the administrator submits the action then the screen shows the returned error message and does not show the other organisation's user as changed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let System Administrators list, search, view, deactivate, and maintain products and create versioned temperature profiles with storage bands, contiguous non-overlapping tiers, allowance or not-permitted designations, a reason, and an effective date no earlier than today, while keeping earlier versions read-only.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A System Administrator searches by product name or code or opens a deactivated product when the API returns matching products and active states then the screen shows matching product records and identifies deactivated products as unavailable for ordering\",\n    \"Given A System Administrator submits an incomplete profile or one with overlapping or gapped tiers when the administrator attempts to save then the screen shows the validation error returned by the API and does not show the product as saved\",\n    \"Given A System Administrator submits a valid profile with tiers, reason, and effective date when the profile change is submitted then the request includes the profile tiers, reason, and effective date and the screen shows the new profile version returned by the API\",\n    \"Given A product has multiple profile versions when a user opens profile history then the screen lists earlier versions with their returned values, reason, effective date, and creator where returned, and provides no edit controls for earlier versions\",\n    \"Given A System Administrator deactivates a product when the API returns the updated product status then the screen shows the product as deactivated\",\n    \"Given A System Administrator enters a profile effective date before today when the administrator attempts to save the profile then the screen shows a validation error and no profile-save request is sent\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a temperature-profile version takes effect, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the new version and API-returned recalculated budgets, decisions, and current statuses for stock still held from its effective date onward, show earlier quality decisions as unchanged, and show resulting order, box, and route statuses for affected allocated or packed stock.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API returns a new effective profile version and recalculated values for stock still held from the effective date onward when a user opens the profile and affected stock views then the screen shows the new version's effective date and the returned budget and decision values\",\n    \"Given A profile version has an effective date of today or later and the API returns an earlier quality decision for affected stock when a user opens the profile and affected stock views then the screen shows the earlier decision's returned values and status unchanged and does not show a recalculated earlier decision\",\n    \"Given A System Administrator submits a profile change with a reason and effective date when the API returns the updated profile and affected-stock results then the screen shows the new version, reason, effective date, and returned recalculated budget and decision values\",\n    \"Given A profile version takes effect and the API returns recalculation results for allocated, packed, or routed stock still held from the effective date onward when an authorized user opens or refreshes the affected order, box, or route then the screen shows the returned allocation, box, and route statuses and any returned action-required message or handover restriction\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a Warehouse Operator records a receipt, the Meridian responsive web app shall capture product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, and storage location and show returned quarantine status and inbound temperature information before a release decision.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Warehouse Operator opens the receipt form when the form is displayed then the screen shows fields for product, lot number, expiry date, quantity, supplier, cold room, and shelf\",\n    \"Given The API accepts a receipt with an inbound logger file when the operator submits the receipt then the screen shows the receipt record, Quarantined status, submitted receipt details, and returned inbound readings and budget use when available\",\n    \"Given The API refuses a receipt with an expired lot date or missing required field when the operator submits the receipt then the screen shows the returned error message beside the relevant field and no saved receipt is displayed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide inbound logger-file upload and display returned temperature history and budget use, validate separate image or PDF receipt-evidence files, and accept logger exports in the supplier's documented format.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Warehouse Operator uploads an inbound logger file in the configured supplier interface format when the receipt is submitted then the request includes the uploaded logger file and the screen shows the returned inbound readings and budget use before release controls\",\n    \"Given A Warehouse Operator uploads a logger file rejected by the API when the upload response is displayed then the screen shows the returned file error message and no successful-upload indicator\",\n    \"Given An operator uploads a separate receipt-evidence image or PDF larger than 10 MB or a separate receipt-evidence file that is not an image or PDF when the operator attempts to submit the receipt then the screen shows a validation error and no saved receipt is displayed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When quality staff review a receipt or excursion, the Meridian responsive web app shall present available release or disposition actions and show decision states returned by the API, including separate proposal and approval steps for not-permitted-range dispositions.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A quarantined receipt is opened by a Quality Officer when the receipt review page renders then the screen shows returned receipt data, temperature-budget use, and release decision controls\",\n    \"Given A receipt is within 30 days of expiry on arrival or the API refuses release when a Quality Officer opens or submits the release decision then the screen shows the reason returned by the API and does not display the stock as released\",\n    \"Given A Quality Officer proposes a disposition for stock exposed to a not-permitted range when the proposal is submitted then the request includes the proposed disposition and reason and the screen shows the proposal awaiting a different Quality Manager's approval\",\n    \"Given The proposing person attempts to approve, or a user without the Quality Manager role attempts approval when the approval is attempted then the screen shows the returned error message or disables the approval control and shows the decision as unapproved\",\n    \"Given A different Quality Manager approves or rejects a pending disposition when the API returns the final decision then the screen shows the returned decision, decision-maker, and decision status\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show on-hand stock with mutually exclusive quantities for available, allocated, quarantined, On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, and Expired statuses, and show returned warehouse, lot, product, receipt, and location details.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API returns on-hand and status quantities for a product, lot, and warehouse when a user opens the stock view then the screen shows the on-hand total and each returned status quantity as a separate field or row, with the quantities summing to the on-hand count\",\n    \"Given The API returns stock rows for multiple lots or warehouses when a user filters the stock list then the screen shows only rows matching the selected filter values\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When portions of received stock have different temperature histories, the Meridian responsive web app shall show them as separate handling units with their returned quantity, history, and tier-budget use and remaining.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A received lot is divided into handling units with different temperature histories when a user opens the lot's handling-unit view then the screen shows separate rows or records with each unit's returned quantity, history, and budget values\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide stock-movement forms and show the returned movement record with source and destination locations, quantity, actor, and time.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Warehouse Operator moves stock between shelves or cold rooms when the operator submits the move and opens its result then the request includes the source and destination and the screen shows the returned movement record with actor, time, and quantity fields\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Customer Administrators maintain their organisation's saved delivery addresses and let System Administrators set the organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life requirement, showing that value read-only to customer users and Dispatchers.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Customer Administrator opens address management when the administrator adds, edits, or removes an address then the screen shows the address list or status returned by the API\",\n    \"Given A System Administrator changes minimum remaining shelf life for a customer organisation when the change is submitted then the request includes the organisation-level value and the screen shows the saved value and response status returned by the API\",\n    \"Given A customer user or Dispatcher opens an order form when the form renders then the screen shows the organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life value without a control to change it per order\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let customer users create orders with one or more product lines, pack quantities, an organisation-saved delivery address, an eligible delivery date, and a choice between delivery of available quantities and complete delivery only.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A customer user opens the order form when the form is displayed then the screen provides fields for at least one product line, a quantity of at least one pack per line, a saved address, requested delivery date, and partial-or-complete delivery preference\",\n    \"Given A customer enters a quantity below one pack or submits an order without a line when the customer submits the form then the screen shows a field error and the request is not sent\",\n    \"Given The API returns eligible delivery dates for the serving warehouse, based on its configured local time, cut-off, working days, and holidays when the customer opens the date selector before or after the configured cut-off then the screen shows only returned eligible dates, applies the next-working-day rule for an order before cut-off and no-earlier-than-the-working-day-after-that rule for an order after cut-off, and identifies the warehouse time zone\",\n    \"Given A customer selects a deactivated product for an order when the product status is returned then the screen shows that the product cannot be ordered and provides no orderable quantity field\",\n    \"Given A customer selects products, quantities, address, date, and fulfillment choice when the customer reviews the order before submission then the screen shows the complete order summary\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When customers view, change, or cancel an order, the Meridian responsive web app shall show order status and allocated and outstanding quantities per line, expose customer change and cancellation controls only before Packed, expose dispatcher cancellation controls when returned as available, and display API outcomes.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API returns an order with line quantities and a status before Packed when the customer opens the order then the screen shows each line's allocated and outstanding quantities and customer change and cancel controls\",\n    \"Given The API returns an order status of Packed or later when the customer opens the order then the screen shows the current status and no customer change or cancel controls\",\n    \"Given A cancellation or change is refused or accepted by the API when the customer submits the action or refreshes the order then the screen shows the returned error or cancellation response, current status, updated quantities, and stock availability count when returned\",\n    \"Given A customer submits an order more than once or retries after a network interruption when the web app sends the submission or retry then the captured request uses the same submission key for the retry and the screen shows one returned order record\",\n    \"Given An order submission is pending when the customer repeats the submission then the screen sends only one order-submission request\",\n    \"Given A Dispatcher opens an order in Packed or later status and the API returns cancellation as available when the Dispatcher opens the order or submits cancellation then the screen shows the dispatcher cancellation control and the returned cancellation response or error message\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show order allocations by line and lot, including returned expiry dates and quantities, expose dispatcher lot-override controls with a required reason and API outcome, and show returned allocation and stock-status outcomes in order, box, and route views.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given An order line is allocated across lots when a Dispatcher or customer opens allocation details then the screen shows each returned lot, expiry date, allocated quantity, line split, and outstanding quantity separately\",\n    \"Given A Dispatcher selects an alternative lot when the override form renders and is submitted then the screen shows a required reason field and the request includes the chosen lot and reason, while the screen shows the accepted allocation or returned refusal message\",\n    \"Given The API reports back order, complete-only status, or no suitable stock when the Dispatcher opens the order then the screen shows the returned allocation status and outstanding quantity\",\n    \"Given Allocated stock becomes On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, or Expired when the order view refreshes then the screen shows the returned removed allocation, replacement allocation outcome, outstanding quantity, and dispatcher message or notification outcome when returned\",\n    \"Given Stock allocated to an order is reported by the API as On Hold, Rejected, Recalled, or Expired after it has been packed or placed on a route when a user opens or refreshes the affected order, box, or route view then the screen shows the returned stock status, resulting allocation and box or route status, and any returned action-required message or handover restriction\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Warehouse Operators pack stock into shipper boxes by type, associate one logger with each box, and show compatibility, contents, and sealing details returned by the API.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Warehouse Operator opens the packing form when the form renders then the screen provides fields for box type, logger identifier, delivery stop, products, lots, and quantities\",\n    \"Given The operator selects stock, a box type, and logger and submits the packing action when the API returns compatibility results or refuses an incompatible band, box type, missing logger, or already-associated logger then the screen shows the returned compatibility result or error message and does not show an unsuccessful box as sealed\",\n    \"Given A box is ready to be sealed and sealing succeeds when the operator opens the box record then the screen shows exactly one logger requirement and the returned seal time, operator, contents, quantities, and logger\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Dispatchers create and view routes with a date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times and show route-confirmation errors and confirmed-route changes returned by the API, including configured qualified-duration safety margins.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Dispatcher creates a route when the route form is displayed then the screen provides fields for one vehicle, one driver, route date, at least one ordered stop, and planned arrival times\",\n    \"Given The API refuses confirmation because a box exceeds its qualified duration after applying the configured safety margin, which defaults to 4 hours when the Dispatcher views the result then the screen shows the refused status, affected box, returned overage amount, and returned configured safety-margin value\",\n    \"Given A confirmed route is changed before the driver has left for an affected stop when the Dispatcher reorders or moves the stop then the request identifies the changed route and the screen shows returned stop order, schedule details, and driver notification status when returned\",\n    \"Given A driver opens a changed confirmed route when the route view is displayed then the screen shows the changed stop or schedule details returned by the API\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show temperature histories for boxes, cold rooms, and lots as charts and tables with returned readings, applicable bands, excursions, gaps, and reading flags or silence status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API returns temperature history when a user opens the history page then the screen provides chart and table views with readings positioned by event or reading time, band bounds, excursion markers, and visible gaps\",\n    \"Given The API returns duplicate, delayed, out-of-order, future-dated, pre-seal, or otherwise flagged readings when the history is displayed then the screen shows returned reading times and flags, identifies invalid-for-calculation readings, and displays returned history in time order without presenting excluded readings as calculation inputs\",\n    \"Given A user switches between chart and table views when the API returns the same history data then the screen shows the corresponding returned history in each view\",\n    \"Given The API returns gateway batch readings or inbound logger-file reading results when a user opens the relevant device or receipt history then the screen displays the returned readings and associated device or receipt\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall show excursions, handling-unit budget use and remaining allowances, returned alerts, and returned hold and decision statuses for affected devices and stock.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API returns an excursion and its affected handling units when a user opens excursion or budget details then the screen shows returned excursion start, end, readings, closure status, affected units, and used and remaining amounts by tier\",\n    \"Given The API returns an open excursion, handling units, and hold statuses when a Quality Officer opens the excursion view then the screen shows affected handling units, tier budgets, and returned hold statuses\",\n    \"Given The API returns a remaining-budget warning, exhausted tier, or not-permitted-range alert when a user opens alerts or quality status then the screen shows the returned alert category and affected stock or device\",\n    \"Given The API returns an alert for silence, excursion, low or exhausted budget, not-permitted range, or corrected excursion when an intended user opens alert history then the screen shows returned alert type, affected device or stock, recipient role and delivery metadata when returned, plus corrected excursion or budget status when present\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the API returns an unresolved temperature-history gap affecting stock, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the gap, review status, and stock status returned by the API without inferring an On Hold status from the gap or displaying an estimated temperature tier.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API returns an unresolved temperature-history gap for affected stock, its review status, and its stock status when a Quality Officer opens the quality status then the screen shows the gap, review status, and returned stock status without estimating a temperature tier\",\n    \"Given The API returns an unresolved gap flagged for review and a stock status of Available, with no other hold reason returned when a user opens the affected stock detail then the screen shows the Available status and review flag and does not show the stock as On Hold because of the gap\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When the API returns an unresolved temperature-history gap affecting stock, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the returned stock status and budget values without presenting an estimated charge to an unobserved temperature tier.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API returns an unresolved temperature-history gap affecting stock, along with stock status and budget values when a user opens the affected stock detail then the screen shows the returned stock status and budget values without presenting an estimated charge to an unobserved tier\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When corrected temperature history identifies an excursion affecting stock already delivered, the Meridian responsive web app shall show the returned quality-review case to the relevant customer and staff users.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given The API returns a quality-review case linked to a delivered customer order when the customer or authorized staff user opens the related order or case then the screen shows the returned case status and affected delivered line or stock details\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide an installable, responsive driver experience that caches the current workday's assigned route, queues supported loading and delivery actions for synchronization when connectivity returns, retains unsynchronized actions tied to the originating driver across sign-out and workday end, synchronizes those actions only after that same driver signs in again, clears cached route and delivery data when the driver signs out, the workday ends, or access is refused, erases or marks queued actions rejected when the API refuses access or reports the account disabled, and shows stale-route and queued-action outcomes returned by the API.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A driver has opened today's assigned route while connected and then loses connectivity when the driver opens the cached route then the screen shows the route, stops, and delivery details while offline\",\n    \"Given A driver records a supported action while offline when the action is saved without a connection then the screen shows the action as queued and retains its entered values until synchronization is attempted\",\n    \"Given The originating driver signs in again with an enabled account and reconnects when queued actions synchronize then the screen shows the returned synchronization result for each queued action\",\n    \"Given A queued action is submitted and the API reports that the originating driver's account is disabled or access is refused when the synchronization response is displayed then the screen shows the returned rejection message or error, marks the action as not accepted or synchronized, and shows it as rejected or no longer queued, with no later synchronization request for that action\",\n    \"Given A Dispatcher changes a cached route or cancels an order while the driver is offline and the API returns the updated route or order on reconnection when the driver refreshes or synchronizes the cached work then the screen identifies the cached route or stop as stale, shows the returned changed route or cancellation status, and does not present a removed stop or cancelled order as actionable\",\n    \"Given A queued loading or handover action refers to a moved or removed stop or a cancelled order when the action synchronizes and the API returns an acceptance or refusal then the screen shows the returned result for that action and does not mark a refused handover as completed or accepted\",\n    \"Given The browser has cached route or delivery data, including recipient details when the driver signs out, the cached workday ends, or an API response reports refused access or a disabled account, and the driver next opens the driver experience then the screen shows the sign-in or access-denied page and no cached route, stop, delivery, or recipient details\",\n    \"Given One or more actions remain queued after the originating driver signs out or the cached workday ends, and a different user signs in on the same browser when that different user opens the driver experience or reconnects then the screen shows no originating driver's route, recipient details, or queued-action details, and the browser sends no synchronization request for the originating driver's actions\",\n    \"Given One or more actions remain queued after the originating driver signs out or the cached workday ends when that same driver signs in again with an enabled account and reconnects then the synchronization request uses that driver's authenticated identity and the screen shows the returned result for each queued action\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"When a driver records a delivery handover, the Meridian responsive web app shall capture the recipient's name, explicit electronic acknowledgment, quantities handed over, and any refusal or partial-delivery reason, and show outstanding quantities and returned delivery status.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A driver opens a delivery handover form when the form is displayed then the screen shows a recipient-name field and explicit electronic acknowledgment control and does not require a drawn signature\",\n    \"Given A driver submits a handover when the web app sends the handover then the captured request contains recipient name, acknowledgment value, and handed-over quantities\",\n    \"Given A delivery is refused or only partly completed when the driver records the handover then the request includes delivered and undelivered quantities and the reason, and the screen shows the returned outstanding quantity\",\n    \"Given Undelivered stock is returned to a warehouse when the API returns the warehouse receipt and any required quality-check result then the screen shows the returned receipt and quality status and shows stock as available only when the API reports it available\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall let Quality Managers start recalls by selecting affected lots and providing a reason, view and manage recall records, and close recalls, and let customer users submit a quantity and stated disposition for each affected delivery, showing returned reconciliation and stock-block information.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A Quality Manager opens a recall record when the recall detail is displayed then the screen lists returned lot locations, affected deliveries, quantities, and remaining stock reported as blocked\",\n    \"Given A customer user opens an affected delivery recall response form when the form is displayed then the screen provides fields for response, quantity, and stated disposition for each delivery and returned quantity categories for locating, using, returning, disposing of, or otherwise accounting for units\",\n    \"Given A customer submits a recall quantity reconciliation when the API returns the response status then the screen shows submitted quantities, stated dispositions, and returned accounted-for status without requiring supporting-document upload\",\n    \"Given A recall has unreconciled quantities when a Quality Manager opens its progress page then the screen shows the outstanding quantity count and affected customer responses returned by the API\",\n    \"Given A Quality Manager starts a recall for one or more lots when the Quality Manager selects the lots, enters a reason, and submits the recall then the request includes the selected lots and reason, and the screen shows the recall record and status returned by the API\",\n    \"Given A Quality Manager closes a recall when the Quality Manager submits the close action then the screen shows the recall status returned by the API\",\n    \"Given The API refuses a recall start or close action when the Quality Manager submits that action then the screen shows the returned error message and does not show the recall as successfully started or closed\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide filtered on-screen operational lists and CSV export, and show creator and last-changer identity and timestamps as read-only metadata where returned.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user opens a supported operational list and applies filters when the user requests CSV export then the screen shows the filtered record list and the downloaded CSV file contains the displayed or filtered records\",\n    \"Given The API returns creator and last-change metadata for a record when an authorized user or Auditor opens the record then the screen shows returned actor and timestamp fields as read-only values\"\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide English and Arabic portal content and render Arabic pages right to left.\",\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    \"Given A user selects Arabic when the user opens a staff, customer, or driver page then the screen shows Arabic text with right-to-left page direction\",\n    \"Given A user selects English when the user opens a portal page then the screen shows English text with left-to-right page direction\"\n   ]\n  }\n ],\n \"nfrs\": [\n  \"Every portal page reflows for phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow layouts.\",\n  \"Main staff, customer, and driver web flows conform to WCAG 2.1 Level AA.\",\n  \"The responsive portals support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.\",\n  \"The web portal supports the stated first-year user and record volume and displays data from the stated simultaneous device volume.\"\n ]\n}\n</artifact>\n\nRestate the change."}